💡 **SUGGESTION: `warnInlineFallbackIfLarge` dereferences `io.log` unguarded**

```js
function warnInlineFallbackIfLarge(io, attempt, putOpts) {
    if (Number(attempt) <= 1 && String(putOpts.json).length >= 96000) {
        io.log('::warning::file_write unavailable — inline argv PUT fallback (E2BIG risk at >=96 KB payloads)');
    }
}
```

`putTokenContents` passes the **raw** io through, and its own guards are defensive everywhere else (`io && typeof io.write === 'function'`, `tryExec(io && io.exec, …)`). But this path calls `io.log(...)` directly: a caller invoking the exported `putTokenContents` (or `publishTokenUsage`) with an io that has `exec` but no `log`, on a payload ≥ 96 KB, gets a `TypeError: io.log is not a function` instead of a degraded publish — breaking the module's documented "never throws" posture (`token_usage_publish.js`: "Never throws — skip and gave-up are statuses, not errors").

Production `buildIo` always supplies `log`, so this is latent, not live. Cheap hardening:

```js
function warnInlineFallbackIfLarge(io, attempt, putOpts) {
    if (Number(attempt) <= 1 && String(putOpts.json).length >= 96000 &&
        io && typeof io.log === 'function') {
        io.log('::warning::file_write unavailable — inline argv PUT fallback (E2BIG risk at >=96 KB payloads)');
    }
}
```

